        "thinking": "Almost all skill service methods call `ensureSkillInventoryCurrent`, which uses FS. These will fail at runtime (not crash at import time, since the FS shim is used). This is expected behavior - these routes will throw an error about FS not being available.\n\nThe `GET /api/companies/:companyId/skills` (list) in `cf-extra-routes.ts` bypasses `ensureSkillInventoryCurrent` and does a direct DB query, so it will work fine. The other skill routes (detail, create, delete) won't work in CF, which is acceptable.\n \nThe cf-extra-routes Hono routes are registered before the catch-all, so they take priority over any overlapping routes from the bridge's compiled routes list. This means the direct DB query route will handle requests correctly without conflict.\n\nI'm reconsidering whether to include `companySkillRoutes` via the bridge at all—most of its methods depend on the filesystem and will fail. Returning 500 for FS-dependent operations is worse than 501 since it's confusing rather than clearly communicating unavailability in this deployment. I should exclude it entirely. However, `accessRoutes` is different since many of its routes like members and invites don't require filesystem access.\n\nLooking through the access routes, most are pure database operations—company members, invites, join request approvals. The DNS-dependent routes are just invite resolution test routes, not core functionality. I need to check which specific routes in access.ts actually use DNS to see if the rest can safely be bridged.",
